  "hypothesis": "Matched software-policy A/B comparisons and LOO ablations on the run-1 100 MHz image evaluate GEMM 16-wide vs 32-wide column layout, Mode B vs single-role pipelining, and 3-core vs 1-core execution under identical hardware conditions.",
  "competing_explanations": [
    "observed cycle deltas reflect unmodeled host submission overhead rather than device execution",
    "residual device state between runs alters cache allocations",
    "thermal throttling on shared U280 affects frequency or latency"
  ],
  "expected_counter_changes": [
    "32-column layout increases fragment count and cycle cost for irregular shapes",
    "Mode B overlaps transfer and compute without doubling register pressure",
    "3 cores distribute grid tasks proportionally across SLRs"
  ],
  "expected_observations": [
    "all policy variations pass numerical correctness against independent CPU references",
    "16-column conservative layout default is nonregressive across shapes",
    "single-role pipeline shows increased cycle count relative to Mode B"
  ],
